# Beat: guided walk through bob/logfile against googleapis.desc,
# with the overrides from alice/app.desc already loaded.
#
# Invocation:
#   protolens --descriptor-set $PROTOTEXT_GOOGLEAPIS_SET bob/logfile \
#       --load-overrides alice/overrides \
#       --script beats/googleapis.desc
#
# Re-pin (must print nothing):
#   protolens --descriptor-set $PROTOTEXT_GOOGLEAPIS_SET bob/logfile \
#       --load-overrides alice/overrides \
#       --script beats/googleapis.desc script \
#     | grep 'error:'

title: The logfile, googleapis.desc

steps:
  - text: |
      bob/logfile — reopened against the full googleapis descriptor set.

      Our overrides are back. Now let's see what googleapis adds.

      👋 Press `2` to unfold.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 1"]
    node: /
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - visible: /3/4

  - text: |
      Fields 6 and 7 now have heat cues — googleapis knows them.

      Field 7: hover the cue.
      ComputeRoutesResponse. The app also calls the Routes API.

      👋 Press `t`, commit ComputeRoutesResponse v2.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/4
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /3/4 google.maps.routing.v2.ComputeRoutesResponse

  - text: |
      Field 6: ComputeRoutesRequest. Symmetric.

      👋 Press `t`, commit ComputeRoutesRequest v2.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - type: /3/3 google.maps.routing.v2.ComputeRoutesRequest

  - text: |
      👌 The log is fully typed.

      But those amber cues are still there.
      Something is wrong with the encoding. Let's look closer 🔍

      👋 Unfold compute_routes_request.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - visible: /3/3/3

  - text: |
      travel_mode: amber diamond + `ohb` annotation.
      ohb = OverHangingBytes: the DRIVE value (1) is encoded with too many bytes.

      Weird...

      👋 Press `w` for wire-level detail.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/3/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - wire: /3/3/3

  - text: |
      Five bytes for the value 1. Canonical would be one byte (0x01).
      This is probably not accidental.

      👋 Press `w` to close wire view.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/3 1", "/3/3 1", "/4 1"]
    node: /3/3/3
    wire_line: /3/3/3
    select_line: true
    advance_when:
      - not:
        - wire: /3/3/3

  - text: |
      One more thing. Back to the shadowed field in the SearchTextRequest.

      Hover the heat cue at the left edge.
      protolens thinks this string might be a google.rpc.Status message.

      👋 Press Enter to commit the google.rpc.Status override.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /1/3/1
    select_line: true
    command: override /1/3/1 --as google.rpc.Status --cardinality optional --field-name status
    advance_when:
      - type: /1/3/1 google.rpc.Status

  - text: |
      🚨 The shadowed field is a google.rpc.Status —
      and it contains an API key 😠

      👋 Press space to step.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/3 Z"]
    node: /1/3/1
    select_node: true
    search: 'value: ".*"'

  - text: |
      Let's export the full logfile as prototext
      and send our findings to Bob.

      👋 Press Enter.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /
    command: export --prototext alice/logfile.all.node.pb
    advance_when:
      - file_exists: alice/logfile.all.node.pb

  - text: |
      👋 Press Enter to quit.

    heat_cues: findings
    fold: ["/ 2", "/1/1 Z"]
    node: /
    command: quit
